response:
Sure. There are two main types of loops:

for loop

The for loop essentially says “for each item in the sequence of values that I’m testing, execute the code inside of this block.”

while loop

The while loop essentially says “as long as the condition is true, execute the code inside of this block.”

So, if I run a for loop, I’ll run it over and over again, for each item in the sequence of values that I’m testing. For example:

int i = 0;

while (i < 5) {
    doSomething();
    i++;
}

In this case, I’m testing the value of i, and if it’s less than five, I’m executing the code inside of the loop.  Since the loop will continue to execute as long as it can determine that i is less than five, this code will execute over and over again.

